From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:37:52 +0000
Subject: Do not block the first frame for the new tab page

On a phone, a cold start whose first tab is expected to be the new tab
page holds every draw of the browser window until the native library,
the profile, the saved tabs and the new tab page itself are ready. The
hold exists for a new tab page that draws the location bar inside the
page: without it, the toolbar's own location bar would show for a moment
first. This new tab page never draws the location bar inside the page.
The toolbar keeps its location bar on the new tab page, so the hold
hides no change of the location bar. It mainly keeps the system splash
screen up about a second longer than a start on a web page.

Skip the hold for the new tab page. The window now draws the toolbar as
soon as the layout is inflated, as it already does when the first tab is
a web page, and the new tab page appears when it is ready. In a light
theme the toolbar and the status bar then change once to the background
color of the new tab page. The holds for incognito restore, activity
recreation and the tab layout do not change.

